BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ROMANCE IN THE CITY WRITING WORKSHOP
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260608T203000
UID:bm-5435720260608@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/SPECIAL_G
 UEST.png?cb=1779283484
DESCRIPTION:[Workshop]\nROMANCE IN THE CITY WRITING WORKSHOP WITH LEANNE T
 OSHIKO SIMPSON\nBack by popular demand!  An evening of city romance\, unfo
 rgettable characters\, and slow-burn chemistry.\nStreetcars at dusk\, hidd
 en cafés\, chance encounters\, and summer nights that change everything 
 — Toronto is full of places where love stories begin. Get ready for an  
 interactive writing workshop on building chemistry\, unforgettable charact
 ers\, and city romance. Includes prompts\, discussion\, Q&A\, and a specia
 l guest: Lavanya Lakshmi\, author of the upcoming novel\nLeave and Come Ba
 ck.\nLeanne Toshiko Simpson teaches creative writing and literature\nat th
 e University of Toronto. Her debut novel\,\nNever BeenBetter\n\, was named
  one of CBC’s Best Books of 2024\,\nand was featured on Good Morning Ame
 rica and in\nElle\nCanada\, Toronto Star\,\nand\nThe Seattle Times\n.\nTic
 ket price includes:\n A two-hour writing workshop  A glass of wine (or non
 -alcoholic beverage) to enjoy during the workshop A $20 book credit\, usab
 le for that night only.  Curated list of writing resources from Leanne.\n
 GET YOUR TICKETS HERE!
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
